## Native libraries (not Rust crates)

These C and C++ libraries are built from source from the pinned releases in `native-deps.toml` and
are not covered by the crate list above. The full licence texts are in the upstream repositories
linked below, at the pinned release.

- **libjpeg-turbo** (IJG AND BSD-3-Clause AND Zlib): this software is based in part on the work of
  the Independent JPEG Group. The IJG licence requires this acknowledgement in the documentation
  of every product that uses the library. Licence: https://github.com/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/blob/main/LICENSE.md
- **libheif** (LGPL-3.0-or-later): HEIF and HEIC container decoding. Shipped as a separate,
  dynamically linked, replaceable shared library. Source: https://github.com/strukturag/libheif
- **libde265** (LGPL-3.0-or-later): HEVC decoding for libheif, loaded as a plugin, decode only.
  Source: https://github.com/strukturag/libde265
- **dav1d** (BSD-2-Clause): AV1 decoding for AVIF, when shipped. Source: https://code.videolan.org/videolan/dav1d
- **libjxl** (BSD-3-Clause): JPEG XL, when shipped. Source: https://github.com/libjxl/libjxl
- **libwebp** (BSD-3-Clause): WebP encoding, when shipped. Source: https://github.com/webmproject/libwebp
- **ONNX Runtime** (MIT): model inference, when shipped. Source: https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
